{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ECC",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Keep thy foot when thou goest to the house of God, and be more ready to hear, than to give the sacrifice of fools: for they consider not that they do evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not rash with thy mouth, and let not thy heart be hasty to utter ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thing before God: for God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in heaven, and thou upon earth: therefore let thy words be few.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For a dream cometh through the multitude of business; and a fool's voice ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is known",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by a multitude of words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When thou vowest a vow to God, defer not to pay it; for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no pleasure in fools: pay that which thou hast vowed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that thou shouldst not vow, than that thou shouldst vow and not pay.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Suffer not thy mouth to cause thy flesh to sin; neither say thou before the angel, that it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an error: why should God be angry at thy voice, and destroy the work of thy hands?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For in the multitude of dreams and many words ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "divers",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanities: but fear thou God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou seest the oppression of the poor, and violent perversion of judgment and justice in a province, wonder not at the matter: for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " higher than the highest regardeth; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " higher than they.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover, the profit of the earth is for all: the king ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is served by the field.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that loveth silver shall not be satisfied with silver; nor he that loveth abundance with increase: this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " also vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When goods increase, they are increased that eat them: and what good ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the owners of them, saving the beholding ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with their eyes?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sleep of a laboring man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sweet, whether he eateth little or much: but the abundance of the rich will not suffer him to sleep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is a grievous evil ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I have seen under the sun, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "namely",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", riches kept for the owners of them to their hurt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But those riches perish by evil labor: and he begetteth a son, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nothing in his hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As he came into the world, naked shall he return to go as he came, and shall take nothing of his labor, which he may carry away in his hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And this also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a grievous evil, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in all points as he came, so shall he go: and what profit hath he that hath labored for the wind?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All his days also he eateth in darkness, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " much sorrow and wrath with his sickness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which I have seen: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good and comely ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to eat and to drink, and to enjoy the good of all his labor that he taketh under the sun all the days of his life, which God giveth him: for it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his portion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every man also to whom God hath given riches and wealth, and hath given him power to eat of it, and to take his portion, and to rejoice in his labor; this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the gift of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.5.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.5.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he shall not much remember the days of his life; because God answereth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the joy of his heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
